{"encoding": "verislop.autonomous-critique/0.1", "phase": "formalize", "attempt": 1, "request": "Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling\n\nImplement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function. Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values. Use Python standard library only, no external I/O. Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end. Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events. For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,... strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)). Sum only non-null in-range values; count counts these values. A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value. Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first); empty buckets never reset previous. Events before start never seed previous. Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order. Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.\n\nImplement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py. Use only the standard library, no external I/O. The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value. Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.\n\nPublic examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]\n", "clauses": [{"clause_id": "C1", "quote": "Software engineering task D21: Grouped bucket aggregation with causal filling", "refs": []}, {"clause_id": "C2", "quote": "Implement solution.py with a pure solve(data) function.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C3", "quote": "Input and output are JSON-compatible Python values.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C4", "quote": "Use Python standard library only, no external I/O.", "refs": ["S1"]}, {"clause_id": "C5", "quote": "Input {events:[{group:string,time:int,value:int|null}],start:int,end:int,width:positive int,fill:'none'|'previous'}, start<=end.", "refs": ["D1"]}, {"clause_id": "C6", "quote": "Groups are all unique event group names sorted lexicographically, including groups with no in-range events.", "refs": ["O2"]}, {"clause_id": "C7", "quote": "For each group, emit buckets starting start,start+width,...", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C8", "quote": "strictly below end, each covering [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).", "refs": ["O3"]}, {"clause_id": "C9", "quote": "Sum only non-null in-range values;", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C10", "quote": "count counts these values.", "refs": ["O4"]}, {"clause_id": "C11", "quote": "A nonempty bucket has value=sum and becomes previous value.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C12", "quote": "Empty bucket value is null for fill none, or latest previous nonempty bucket sum for fill previous (null before first);", "refs": ["O5"]}, {"clause_id": "C13", "quote": "empty buckets never reset previous.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C14", "quote": "Events before start never seed previous.", "refs": ["I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C15", "quote": "Return [{group,start,count,value}] in group then bucket order.", "refs": ["O6"]}, {"clause_id": "C16", "quote": "Zero sum is a real previous value, duplicates are counted.", "refs": ["O4", "I1"]}, {"clause_id": "C17", "quote": "Implement a pure deterministic Python 3 function solve(data) in solution.py.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C18", "quote": "Use only the standard library, no external I/O.", "refs": ["S1"]}, {"clause_id": "C19", "quote": "The function receives a JSON value and returns a JSON-serializable value.", "refs": ["O1"]}, {"clause_id": "C20", "quote": "Preserve the specified input/output structure and exact ordering.", "refs": ["O6"]}, {"clause_id": "C21", "quote": "Public examples (additional held-out cases will be scored):\n[{\"input\": {\"end\": 5, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 0, \"value\": 2}, {\"group\": \"a\", \"time\": 1, \"value\": -2}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 2, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 2, \"value\": 0}, {\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"a\", \"start\": 4, \"value\": 0}]}, {\"input\": {\"end\": 1, \"events\": [{\"group\": \"z\", \"time\": -1, \"value\": 9}], \"fill\": \"previous\", \"start\": 0, \"width\": 2}, \"output\": [{\"count\": 0, \"group\": \"z\", \"start\": 0, \"value\": null}]}]", "refs": ["O7"]}], "records": [{"id": "D1", "revision": 1, "kind": "entity", "role": "declaration", "statement": "The input is an object with events, start, end, width and fill; each event has a string group, integer time and integer or null value. start and end are integers, width is a positive integer, fill is 'none' or 'previous', and start <= end.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 366, "interpretation": "Specified input structure and domain.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 238}], "scope": ["specified input domain"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["The declared input domain matches the specified field names, types and bounds."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:dadac8bdf730cc5d99a2e31e1eef5d3ac5463538d7b31e78967c929e036351ca", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O1", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Provide a pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data) function in solution.py accepting JSON-compatible Python input and returning a JSON-serializable value.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 134, "interpretation": "Function location, name and purity.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 79}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 186, "interpretation": "JSON-compatible interface.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 135}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1129, "interpretation": "Python 3, purity and determinism.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1053}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1251, "interpretation": "JSON input and serializable output.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1178}], "scope": ["function interface and execution"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["solution.py exposes solve(data).", "Repeated calls with equivalent inputs produce identical results without observable side effects.", "The result is JSON-serializable."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:2c6b4bae4df1d10f3a5df3fd92280249b58f9b47cbfd26c11128e0e0bc6dd5c6", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O2", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Determine groups from every event's group name, deduplicate names and sort them lexicographically, retaining groups whose events are all outside the requested range.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 474, "interpretation": "Group membership and ordering.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 367}], "scope": ["all input events"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Groups equal the lexicographically sorted set of group names in events.", "Out-of-range events still contribute group names.", "An empty events list yields no groups and an empty result."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:2d8d1a5a4b462e8f09ddd0fbf49a3b36581962d7bf5ca8fa8596b89bbc46ed80", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O3", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For each group generate bucket starts start + k*width for all nonnegative integers k whose starts are strictly below end. Each bucket covers [bucketStart,min(bucketStart+width,end)).", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 534, "interpretation": "Bucket start progression for each group.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 475}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 610, "interpretation": "Strict endpoint limit and half-open bucket coverage.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 535}], "scope": ["each group and requested interval"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Every group has exactly the specified ascending bucket starts.", "The final bucket is clipped at end.", "start = end yields no buckets.", "A time at a bucket's upper endpoint belongs to the following bucket if present; a time equal to end belongs to no bucket."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:81e6d65e3f2bd6e6bbdd7e37135e6f59004184bc742f4a080a55664d5d7c249f", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O4", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "For each bucket sum and count all events of its group whose times fall in the bucket and whose values are non-null. Count each duplicate event occurrence separately.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 645, "interpretation": "Non-null in-range aggregation.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 611}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 672, "interpretation": "Count uses the same qualifying values.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 646}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1051, "interpretation": "Duplicates are counted.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 993}], "scope": ["each generated bucket"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["count equals the number of qualifying event occurrences.", "sum equals the exact integer sum of qualifying values.", "Null values and times outside [start,end) contribute neither sum nor count.", "Duplicate occurrences contribute independently.", "A bucket containing only null-valued events has count zero."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:93db820b67a72204841982944a42007568794ac7ce0cacc0fd506c1c96a9f49b", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O5", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "An empty bucket outputs null under fill 'none'. Under fill 'previous', it outputs the latest previous nonempty bucket sum for the same group, or null if none exists.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 852, "interpretation": "Fill modes and initial null behavior.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 733}], "scope": ["buckets with count zero"], "dependencies": [{"id": "D1", "relation": "uses_definition"}, {"id": "I1", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["fill 'none' produces null for every empty bucket.", "fill 'previous' uses the latest preceding nonempty bucket sum.", "Empty buckets before the first nonempty bucket output null.", "A preceding sum of zero fills subsequent empty buckets with zero."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:4e7c9c7c3e44a7016d1a558e37c4e8f6933440b268b7450a75ff178ddf1c9176", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O6", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Return a list of objects with exactly group, start, count and value fields, one per generated group bucket, ordered first by lexicographic group and then ascending bucket start.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 992, "interpretation": "Output record structure and ordering.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 930}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1317, "interpretation": "Exact structure and ordering preservation.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1252}], "scope": ["returned value"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O2", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O3", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "I1", "relation": "uses_proof"}, {"id": "O5", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["Each record has the specified group name, bucket start, qualifying count and computed value.", "The list preserves group then bucket ordering.", "The specified input and output structures are preserved."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:e67504d0cebd4c8d70f1941e60c9a7b0b5cf8f613ed508c0018e1a606c5089a4", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "O7", "revision": 1, "kind": "postcondition", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Match both public examples: the a-group zero-sum bucket has count 2 and value 0 followed by empty buckets at starts 2 and 4 with value 0; the z-group with only a pre-start event has a single bucket at start 0 with count 0 and value null.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1891, "interpretation": "Concrete zero-sum carry-forward and pre-start exclusion examples.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1319}], "scope": ["public example inputs"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O6", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["The first example returns exactly the three specified a-group records.", "The second example returns exactly the specified z-group record."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:e4cb50d77f7006b816c16d205a954380cdd8ebaf4adf4cd2924fefa8fed29778", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "I1", "revision": 1, "kind": "invariant", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Within each group, previous begins unset and tracks the sum of the latest earlier bucket with count greater than zero. Processing a nonempty bucket sets its value and previous to its sum, including zero; empty buckets preserve previous. Events before start never initialize previous.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 732, "interpretation": "Nonempty bucket value and previous update.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 673}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 888, "interpretation": "Empty buckets preserve previous.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 853}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 929, "interpretation": "Pre-start events cannot seed previous.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 889}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1051, "interpretation": "Zero is a valid previous sum.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 993}], "scope": ["ascending bucket processing within each group"], "dependencies": [{"id": "O4", "relation": "uses_proof"}], "acceptance_criteria": ["previous is initially unset independently for each group.", "A count-positive bucket outputs its sum and updates previous even when its sum is zero.", "A count-zero bucket leaves previous unchanged.", "Pre-start events cannot seed previous."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:00e366f11948873237254a96655142bac12ede1b7566f2b7e700a526343d11ba", "blocked_by": []}, {"id": "S1", "revision": 1, "kind": "safety_property", "role": "guarantee", "statement": "Use only the Python standard library and perform no external I/O.", "required": true, "source_refs": [{"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 237, "interpretation": "Library and I/O restrictions.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 187}, {"document_hash": "sha256:1e1a8ccb008420489eab50ddfe73e1632b674ccb2202aeced608a233f7ac3296", "document_ref": "tasks/D21/prompt.txt", "end_byte": 1177, "interpretation": "Repeated library and I/O restrictions.", "origin": "explicit", "start_byte": 1130}], "scope": ["implementation and all solve executions"], "dependencies": [], "acceptance_criteria": ["No third-party library is required.", "Execution performs no external I/O."], "origin": "interpreted", "record_digest": "sha256:d18dd460abf91b41fddd2cb11b2fd62e74ba1507c0b3522860999c808322884e", "blocked_by": []}], "lean_source": "-- unparseable formalizer response\n", "formalization": {"error": "unparseable formalizer response: unterminated outer JSON object in the response"}, "profile": null, "statements": {}, "diagnostics": [{"code": "INVALID_CANDIDATE", "severity": "blocking", "message": "unparseable formalizer response: unterminated outer JSON object in the response", "obligations": [], "claims": []}], "previous_critique": null, "raw_formalizer_response": "{\"encoding\":\"verislop.formalizer-ast/0.1\",\"records\":{\"Event\":{\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"group\",\"sort\":\"String\"},{\"name\":\"time\",\"sort\":\"Int\"},{\"name\":\"value\",\"sort\":{\"option\":\"Int\"}}]},\"Input\":{\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"events\",\"sort\":{\"list\":{\"record\":\"Event\"}}},{\"name\":\"start\",\"sort\":\"Int\"},{\"name\":\"end\",\"sort\":\"Int\"},{\"name\":\"width\",\"sort\":\"Int\"},{\"name\":\"fill\",\"sort\":\"String\"}]},\"Row\":{\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"group\",\"sort\":\"String\"},{\"name\":\"start\",\"sort\":\"Int\"},{\"name\":\"count\",\"sort\":\"Nat\"},{\"name\":\"value\",\"sort\":{\"option\":\"Int\"}}]},\"State\":{\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"previous\",\"sort\":{\"option\":\"Int\"}},{\"name\":\"rows\",\"sort\":{\"list\":{\"record\":\"Row\"}}}]},\"Stats\":{\"fields\":[{\"name\":\"count\",\"sort\":\"Nat\"},{\"name\":\"sum\",\"sort\":\"Int\"}]}},\"symbols\":{\"solve\":{\"args\":[{\"record\":\"Input\"}],\"result\":{\"list\":{\"record\":\"Row\"}},\"body\":{\"tag\":\"list_foldl\",\"value\":{\"tag\":\"list_sort\",\"value\":{\"tag\":\"list_unique\",\"value\":{\"tag\":\"list_map\",\"value\":{\"tag\":\"field\",\"sort\":\"Input\",\"field\":\"events\",\"value\":{\"tag\":\"var\",\"index\":0}},\"function\":{\"sort\":{\"record\":\"Event\"},\"body\":{\"tag\":\"field\",\